const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"比较自己的过去，而不是同伴排名",en:"Compare an asset with its own past, not its peers"},body:{zh:"时间序列动量关注同一资产过去与未来收益的关系，横截面动量则比较资产相对同伴的表现。即使两者都使用过去收益，它们的基准与问题不同。市场中所有资产同时上涨时，一个资产仍可能在自身历史意义上上涨、却在横截面落后。",en:"Time-series momentum relates an asset's own past and future returns; cross-sectional momentum compares its performance with peers. Their benchmarks differ even when both use past returns. An asset can rise in absolute terms while lagging a broadly rising market."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §1",en:"2012 journal article · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"研究输入是合约收益，不是拼接价格图",en:"The input is contract returns, not a stitched price chart"},body:{zh:"论文逐日计算流动性较高合约的超额收益，再将收益复合为可比较的序列。换月时的两个价格可能因为交割日期不同而有价差；直接连接价格并求涨跌，会把合约差异误认为持有收益。收益定义应先于任何历史比较。",en:"The article compounds daily excess returns from liquid contracts into comparable series. Contracts with different delivery dates can have different prices at a roll. Joining their prices and taking changes can mistake a contract difference for a holding-period return."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §2.1 · p. 231",en:"2012 journal article · §2.1 · p. 231"}}},{title:{zh:"不同资产先处理波动尺度",en:"Reconcile volatility scales across assets"},body:{zh:"不同合约的波动大小差异很大，未经处理的汇总可能被少数高波动资产主导。作者用事先估计的波动率将收益放在相近尺度上。这个变换改变比较的权重，不等于提高了原始收益，也不保证每个资产未来风险完全相同。",en:"Volatility differs substantially across contracts, so unscaled aggregation can be dominated by a few volatile instruments. The paper uses ex ante volatility to put returns on comparable scales. This changes comparison weights; it does not improve raw returns or equalize future risk perfectly."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §2.4",en:"2012 journal article · §2.4"}}},{title:{zh:"风险估计必须早于所评价的收益",en:"The risk estimate must precede the evaluated return"},body:{zh:"波动率估计使用滞后平方收益，并在评价当期收益时采用上一时点的估计。这个时间顺序避免把当前结果反馈进事前风险尺度。用整个样本统一标准化虽然方便，却会与原文事先可得信息的含义不同，必须明确区分。",en:"Volatility is estimated from lagged squared returns, using the prior estimate for the current return. That ordering avoids feeding the evaluated outcome into its ex ante scale. Full-sample normalization would have a different information meaning and must be distinguished."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §2.4 · equation (1)",en:"2012 journal article · §2.4 · equation (1)"}}},{title:{zh:"商业与非商业分类不是动机的直接观测",en:"Trader classifications do not directly observe motives"},body:{zh:"研究使用CFTC的商业与非商业交易者分类讨论持仓，但原文承认商业交易者也可能进行投机，分类覆盖也并非所有合约一致。这些标签是申报口径，不能直接证明每个账户的真实目的；周度持仓也不是逐笔成交记录。",en:"CFTC commercial and non-commercial categories support the position analysis, but commercial traders can also speculate and coverage differs across contracts. These reporting labels do not prove individual motives. Weekly positions are not transaction-by-transaction trading records."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §2.2",en:"2012 journal article · §2.2"}}},{title:{zh:"多资产面板仍共享同一时间冲击",en:"A multi-asset panel still shares shocks across time"},body:{zh:"回归将不同合约与日期组合起来，同时按月份聚类计算推断，以考虑同月资产间的相关。合约数量增加不等于增加同等数量的独立历史。对历史持续性的解释，还应与样本选择、预测期限和未使用样本中的表现分开讨论。",en:"The pooled regressions account for common monthly dependence through time clustering. More contracts do not supply an equal number of independent histories. Interpretation of persistence must remain separate from sample selection, forecast horizons and evidence from untouched observations."},reference:{url:"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf",label:{zh:"2012年期刊版 · §3.1",en:"2012 journal article · §3.1"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"这里讨论历史研究的测量与推断，不提供交易信号或组合。期货超额收益、现货价格和合约拼接不是同一对象；历史统计关系不保证未来表现。",en:"This guide concerns measurement and inference, not signals or portfolios. Futures excess returns, spot prices and contract stitching are different objects; historical associations do not guarantee future performance."}};export{e as default};
